<title>FINLAND: OKOBANK says unwise to rush markka-ERM link.</title>
<headline>OKOBANK says unwise to rush markka-ERM link.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland should not make a hasty decision on linking the markka to Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM), OKOBANK said in a bond market review received on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;While parliaments in Germany, France and many other EU countries are discussing their next year's budgets, it is not wise to make a hasty decision regarding the ERM link of the Finnish markka,&quot; OKOBANK said.</p>
<p>If the budget plans are rejected by the German or French parliaments, this would put markets under pressure as Economic and Monetary Union would no longer be guaranteed, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;In such an event, it would be wise to stay out of any kind of mechanisms, as all possible pressures will hit the northernmost EU rim hardest,&quot; OKOBANK said.</p>
<p>The government was expected to give an idea of the reasons that will guide its decision on whether to link the markka to ERM at parliament's question-and-answer session later on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom + 358 - 0 - 680 50 240</p>
